{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact b5d9c26d42270f9e48b29ebb327f78e12c4fea8f (tree f44f9495536e8c06b779fe3c3b13deddb8573562), against Main afe0c3190d500f5936e7bd711be67ee4b980b4e0.\n\n1. P2 — Make pickup representable by the declared query contract (notes/2026-10-21-roles-flow-and-instances.md:58, 88-98). The preset specifies one canonical dap items query that selects eligible work. Its current wire type has one type plus states/IDs, with no party predicates or joins (packages/contract/src/item-query.ts:17-29; docs/cli.md:438). The planner needs both intent and report items, and its no-commitment/requester predicates cannot be expressed. The builder also needs performer/offeree and held-hold checks that this query does not express. Define pickup as bounded candidate queries plus named adapter eligibility checks, or name a separately commissioned query extension. Give each preset its concrete types/states, party/related-item checks, coverage and continuation policy. Keep the distinction between an incomplete read and no eligible work. The existing team note section 5 already separates candidate reading from eligibility; the new preset shape must support that sequence.\n\n2. P2 — Specify an admission path for every preset before dispatch (primary note:86-109; amended team note:237-255). The latter requires an admitted app claim before starting an attempt. Planner and checker name no claim. Builder names take-hold for offered and accepted commitments, but take-hold requires accepted state and performer authority (issue.ts:530-549), while accept appears among acts on already claimed work. An offered commitment therefore cannot pass the documented dispatch sequence. Also, offer only checks that the goal is open (issue.ts:350-364), so it does not exclude duplicate planner offers; check/check-error settle results after the expensive work rather than claiming a requested job beforehand (change.ts:1038-1116). Define the offered-to-accepted-to-held sequence, 